<title>USA: Calif. names new deputy insurance commissioner.</title>
<headline>Calif. names new deputy insurance commissioner.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The California Department of Insurance on Tuesday said Keith Newman was appointed deputy commissioner of its fraud division.</p>
<p>In his new position, Newman will be responsible for managing the criminal investigation programs of the fraud division, which consists of a staff of 229.</p>
<p>Newman, a former division commander of the California Highway Patrol, replaces Barbara Dotta, who is returning to the District Attorney's office in Fresno.</p>
